cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use XStream in academic work, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "XStream: an integrated CT acquisition and reconstruction workstation with software-defined continuous-rotation timing"
abstract: >-
  XStream is a single-workstation system that integrates motorized CT acquisition,
  pipelined storage, local GPU reconstruction and automated provenance recording for
  parallel-beam CT at a synchrotron fast-imaging beamline. For continuous-rotation
  (fly) scanning with a commercial free-running sCMOS camera that provides no
  position-synchronized triggering, it implements a deterministic timing plan:
  on-line calibration of the frame period, derivation of the maximum angular velocity
  from an explicit edge-blur constraint, and alignment of the frame stride to an
  integer multiple of the calibrated period.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/puluotac/XStream"
url: "https://github.com/puluotac/XStream"
